{
  "ideas": [
    {
      "id": 21,
      "name": "Geyser Field",
      "approach": "handmade",
      "approachWhy": "Every geyser layout depends on its beat, launch height and landing spot fitting together, and a random mix easily makes a launch that can't reach or a beat that never lines up. A small hand-tuned set that the tests check is safer and still gives lots of variety.",
      "engine": {
        "have": [
          "bounce motion: throws the local player straight up at a set power (TRAMPOLINE 62 = about 10 studs, CANNON 75 = about 14 studs)",
          "flip motion: a duty cycle on server time (frac(t / period + phase) < duty), the same clock a geyser beat needs",
          "melt motion: a per-player trigger when you stand on a part, then a timed reset (the base for a one-shot geyser)",
          "ghost parts for see-through columns, red hazard look, disc shapes for vents",
          "tests that check gaps and rises against the launch powers"
        ],
        "new": [
          {
            "what": "erupt motion kind: a vent with a beat (period, phase, warn time, blow time, power); during the blow window a player on the vent or inside its column is thrown up, outside it the vent is just floor. Its on/off clock is the same duty + phase timer Updraft (idea 5) plans for its 'lift with an on/off timer'; build that timer once and use it in both",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "one-shot trigger (idea 1 Crusher Alley reuses it for its plates): stepping on the vent starts a short countdown, it blows once, then stays dry for a refill time (melt-style, per player)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "blow strength per beat for Third Time: reuse Crusher Alley's (idea 1) 'pattern' motion (a list of beats, same format as Beat Pads' patterns), with a power on each beat (puff, puff, big)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "column catch: the lift check also covers a player who jumps sideways into the column while it is up (same live-region check Updraft uses for its columns), for Spout Catch and Pit Spouts",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "geyser looks in ObbyFx: rim glow that brightens through the warning, bubbles and steam, a goo column that shoots up and falls back, plus a bubbling sound that gets louder and a whoosh on the blow",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "red hazard geyser: the same erupt motion, its column a red see-through hazard; touching it uses the shared 'hazard touch = back to the start pad' from idea 1",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "test: extend Bounce Chain's (idea 4) launchReaches() with geyser powers and column catches, and add a wait check: every beat leaves a wait of at most about 4 s",
            "size": "S"
          }
        ]
      },
      "readability": "A geyser is a round green goo pool with a rock rim: the rim glows brighter, it bubbles louder and steam rises in the last second before it blows, and then a green goo column shoots up. A hazard geyser is the same pool in red see-through goo, so the player learns 'green column lifts me, red column resets me'.",
      "generator": null,
